WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:06.000
First: an account is kept
on Kerberos, Keep Kerberos.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.125
What must it have?

4
00:00:07.125 --> 00:00:11.095
The answer is b: the authorizing
official's acceptance,

5
00:00:11.095 --> 00:00:14.800
an S P N owner and an end date
no later than D oh eight's.

6
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:20.834
That's Chapter 3's rule for an account
kept on Kerberos; a kept G M S A or

7
00:00:20.834 --> 00:00:26.538
D M S A ends by G 5 instead, and needs
an S P N owner only if it has S P N's.

8
00:00:26.538 --> 00:00:31.376
The check enforces it with N
P I K R B oh five and oh six.

9
00:00:31.376 --> 00:00:35.857
Second: why would this chapter
block a D M S A for svc webfront,

10
00:00:35.857 --> 00:00:38.875
the reason its owner kept it on Kerberos?

11
00:00:38.875 --> 00:00:40.100
The answer is b.

12
00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:43.563
The account is trusted for
unconstrained delegation,

13
00:00:43.563 --> 00:00:48.258
and Microsoft Learn's delegated
managed service account documentation

14
00:00:48.258 --> 00:00:51.875
says that stops working once
a D M S A migration completes.

15
00:00:51.875 --> 00:00:55.627
That's N P I K R B oh four,
and it's why the owner kept

16
00:00:55.627 --> 00:00:59.775
the account on Kerberos
instead of planning a D M S A.

17
00:00:59.775 --> 00:01:02.202
The module page has three more questions,

18
00:01:02.202 --> 00:01:04.700
each linked to the
section that answers it.
